1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:03,040
<i>Like a fairy tale</i>

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,460
<i>It's a sign the story has reached its end</i>

3
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:08,380
<i>Like a single passage taken from</i>

4
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:10,000
<i>A journey that was too long</i>

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,340
<i>Of the evil that once cast a shadow</i>

6
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:14,680
<i>Across this land</i>

7
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:17,010
<i>And the memories of the short journey</i>

8
00:00:17,010 --> 00:00:19,470
<i>With the hero who defeated it</i>

9
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:31,780
<i>The story ends</i>

10
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:34,280
<i>And the hero goes to sleep</i>

11
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:37,110
<i>Leaving this land with</i>

12
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:38,780
<i>Days of peace and quiet</i>

13
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:41,290
<i>The passage of time heartlessly</i>

14
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:43,450
<i>Makes people forget</i>

15
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:46,250
<i>Even the tracks left behind by his life</i>

16
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:48,040
<i>Begin to rust</i>

17
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:49,880
<i>Just the same</i>

18
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,170
<i>Your words and wishes and courage</i>

19
00:00:52,170 --> 00:00:55,510
<i>Are still inside of me</i>

20
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:57,380
<i>And they live on</i>

21
00:00:58,180 --> 00:00:59,930
<i>We chose the same path</i>

22
00:00:59,930 --> 00:01:02,060
<i>That's all it was supposed to be</i>

23
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:03,600
<i>Why is it that at some point</i>

24
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:07,850
<i>I wanted to understand the reason for</i>

25
00:01:07,850 --> 00:01:09,230
<i>The tears that fall down my cheeks</i>

26
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:10,310
<i>Even now</i>

27
00:01:10,310 --> 00:01:12,690
<i>If I retrace the journey we walked together</i>

28
00:01:12,690 --> 00:01:16,240
<i>Even though you're not there</i>

29
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:17,910
<i>I know I'll be able to find it</i>

30
00:01:31,870 --> 00:01:33,500
I see.

31
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:36,690
I remember now.

32
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:39,410
It was Frieren.

33
00:01:41,130 --> 00:01:46,200
The mage who contributed significantly
to humanity's analysis of Zoltraak

34
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:51,100
and slew more demons
than anyone else in history.

35
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:56,060
Frieren the Slayer.

36
00:01:58,420 --> 00:02:01,170
One of the geniuses I despise.

37
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:15,210
You'll have to rest for a while.

38
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:16,600
Thank you.

39
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,360
Hey!

40
00:02:26,730 --> 00:02:28,070
Are you okay?

41
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:32,190
Because of you, I'll survive.

42
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:33,660
You have my thanks.

43
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:41,820
I'll pardon your mage companion as well.

44
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,620
She was right.

45
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:49,190
Now Frieren can return to town.

46
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:51,290
Let's have her defeat Lügner
and the other demon.

47
00:02:51,970 --> 00:02:56,020
Ms. Frieren didn't kill the guard.

48
00:02:56,600 --> 00:03:00,060
I know. The demons did it.

49
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:04,730
More importantly,
that mage's name is Frieren?

50
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:05,550
Yes.

51
00:03:05,990 --> 00:03:09,860
The elven mage who adventured with the Hero?

52
00:03:10,550 --> 00:03:13,690
Then I've committed a grave discourtesy.

53
00:03:14,490 --> 00:03:17,570
The Granat family owes the
party of heroes a debt.

54
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:23,390
When this town was attacked by demons
during my grandfather's rule,

55
00:03:23,390 --> 00:03:25,460
they were the ones who drove them off.

56
00:03:26,270 --> 00:03:27,830
They faced the same enemy as we do now.

57
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:31,260
It was Aura, one of the
Seven Sages of Destruction.

58
00:03:33,610 --> 00:03:36,210
It's been a while, Aura.

59
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:41,200
Indeed, Frieren. About eighty years, I'd say.

60
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:46,960
You're heading to the town
up ahead, aren't you?

61
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:50,460
I'd appreciate it if you turned back.

62
00:03:51,450 --> 00:03:52,380
No.

63
00:03:53,270 --> 00:03:54,130
Why not?

64
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:18,160
Because I have an overwhelming advantage.

65
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,050
Oh?

66
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:25,780
You have more puppets than before.

67
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:31,220
Demon magic must be unbelievably
powerful to control this many.

68
00:04:31,930 --> 00:04:35,970
Humanity's magic could never
dream of reaching such heights.

69
00:04:37,550 --> 00:04:40,740
But your magic couldn't be more disgusting.

70
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:41,810
It makes me want to puke.

71
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:44,740
That's not a nice thing to say.

72
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:47,270
It took a lot of work to gather this many.

73
00:04:56,390 --> 00:04:58,910
I recognize some of those suits of armor.

74
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:04,330
Aura, it seems I must
kill you here after all.

75
00:05:08,650 --> 00:05:10,560
The Scales of Obedience.

76
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:15,530
It's the reason we haven't been able
to defeat Aura in all these years.

77
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:22,490
Her magic allows her to force
others to obey her will.

78
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:25,560
The magics of the Seven Sages of Destruction

79
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:27,990
are beyond human knowledge and reason.

80
00:05:29,150 --> 00:05:33,160
Aura places her own soul
and that of her target on the scales

81
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:35,660
and weighs the magnitude of
their mana against each other.

82
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:40,750
The one with greater mana
gains control of the other,

83
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:47,760
turning them into a puppet for all eternity—
until their body withers to dust.

84
00:05:49,670 --> 00:05:52,520
It's a risky spell, but that's
what makes it powerful.

85
00:05:53,090 --> 00:05:57,670
And in the hands of someone with mana
as tremendous as Aura, it's unbeatable.

86
00:05:58,470 --> 00:06:00,930
Is there no way to counter it?

87
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:07,010
Though the weight of Aura's mana
is enough to fully tip the scales,

88
00:06:07,010 --> 00:06:08,990
the scales themselves do judge fairly.

89
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:13,900
If a soul with greater mana than Aura's
were to be placed on the scales,

90
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:16,540
Aura could be defeated.

91
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:24,350
But they say that hasn't happened
once in the five hundred years

92
00:06:24,350 --> 00:06:27,540
since Aura became a Sage of Destruction.

93
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:31,040
Then there's no way to fight it?

94
00:06:35,450 --> 00:06:37,850
There was.

95
00:06:38,670 --> 00:06:43,550
Those with powerful wills could
temporarily resist the spell.

96
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:50,570
The greater the individual,
the more iron their will.

97
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:53,700
And even then, it was only temporary?

98
00:06:54,050 --> 00:06:56,640
But it was a fatal flaw.

99
00:06:56,640 --> 00:07:00,080
The strong-willed must have been
an obstacle to her.

100
00:07:00,580 --> 00:07:01,570
So...

101
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:09,710
Aura the Guillotine dealt with them in the
most logical way after gaining control.

102
00:07:10,770 --> 00:07:12,720
It's a tragic tale.

103
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:23,430
Well? My immortal army
is powerful, isn't it?

104
00:07:38,050 --> 00:07:39,320
I'm surprised.

105
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:43,320
You dispelled the magic I'd cast on them.

106
00:07:44,110 --> 00:07:46,330
No one's ever done that before.

107
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:53,110
Such powerful dispelling magic must expend
a considerable amount of mana.

108
00:07:53,550 --> 00:07:56,350
Why would you use such a roundabout method?

109
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:02,230
The last time we fought, you blew them away
with flashy spells left and right.

110
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:07,420
Himmel scolded me afterward.

111
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:12,730
Then that's all the more reason
not to do this.

112
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:15,110
Why?

113
00:08:15,670 --> 00:08:17,870
Himmel is long gone, isn't he?

114
00:08:20,270 --> 00:08:22,360
I see. Good.

115
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:27,320
You demons are monsters after all.

116
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,140
I can kill you without mercy.

117
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:30,840
Okay.

118
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:34,170
I've regained most of my mobility.

119
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:38,750
Father, this place is safe, right?

120
00:08:38,750 --> 00:08:42,480
Yes. It's not as strong as the
town's defensive barrier,

121
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:45,470
but there is a barrier around this church.

122
00:08:45,910 --> 00:08:48,180
Then wait here, Graf.

123
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:52,740
Brat, what do you plan to do?

124
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:56,910
Do you think the demons will just leave
if we all hole up in here?

125
00:08:57,520 --> 00:09:00,020
Mr. Stark, are you serious?

126
00:09:01,110 --> 00:09:04,240
We only landed that hit before
because we caught him off guard.

127
00:09:04,630 --> 00:09:07,790
We couldn't find enough of an
opening to finish him off.

128
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:14,070
If we'd kept fighting, we would
have been the ones killed.

129
00:09:15,310 --> 00:09:18,020
Someone's gotta do this, right?

130
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:26,600
You're right. Then let's
do our best together.

131
00:09:28,630 --> 00:09:31,890
No, you go to the guard station.

132
00:09:32,370 --> 00:09:34,370
You need to evacuate the townsfolk.

133
00:09:35,170 --> 00:09:36,860
Then you're going to...

134
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,370
Yeah.

135
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:43,010
I'm going to...

136
00:09:43,010 --> 00:09:46,370
get on my hands and knees
and beg Frieren to return.

137
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:47,960
What?

138
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:54,360
Come on! Having her defeat him
is our only option!

139
00:09:55,350 --> 00:09:58,530
I suppose that's more realistic.

140
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:06,480
The guards will listen to you
if you show them this.

141
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:09,280
Very well.

142
00:10:10,490 --> 00:10:12,150
I'm heading straight out of town.

143
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:15,400
What is it?

144
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:18,290
Your arm is in a terrible state.

145
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:21,780
Can you pass through the castle gate
looking like that?

146
00:10:22,970 --> 00:10:26,820
I'll be fine. This is normal for a warrior.

147
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:28,240
Is there something weird about it?

148
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:33,620
I've never seen a warrior walk
around town with two bloody hands.

149
00:10:33,950 --> 00:10:37,620
You're one to talk. You're
covered in blood, too.

150
00:10:38,830 --> 00:10:41,540
Huh? Whose blood is this?

151
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,130
It's not mine.

152
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:49,180
Hey! What's the matter with—

153
00:10:52,990 --> 00:10:55,520
Mr. Stark, there's mana in this blood.

154
00:10:57,220 --> 00:10:58,160
Fern!

155
00:11:07,090 --> 00:11:07,840
<i>An axe?</i>

156
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:16,850
I don't believe it. Am I dreaming?

157
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:20,020
That was my master's technique.

158
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:27,270
I'd meant to hit your vitals,
but then you went and moved.

159
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:30,970
It wasn't my intention to make you suffer.

160
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:37,600
Why are you surprised?

161
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:42,150
Is it because I'm standing here when
I supposedly suffered a fatal blow?

162
00:11:42,450 --> 00:11:46,150
Or because you didn't detect our approach?

163
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:54,570
You aren't the only one who knows how to
conceal her presence by controlling her mana.

164
00:11:54,930 --> 00:11:57,660
Any demon can do it.

165
00:11:58,630 --> 00:12:05,680
That said, it's hardly fitting
for a battle between mages.

166
00:12:06,570 --> 00:12:08,220
You sure like to talk.

167
00:12:08,700 --> 00:12:10,430
Aren't you going to finish me off?

168
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:15,980
Since I failed to kill you instantly,
I thought I'd ask you some questions.

169
00:12:18,490 --> 00:12:20,720
Or would you rather die right now?

170
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:23,740
Go ahead.

171
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:28,680
Is that boy strong?

172
00:12:29,670 --> 00:12:32,170
He's Eisen the Warrior's best student.

173
00:12:32,790 --> 00:12:35,460
I see. How unfortunate.

174
00:12:36,110 --> 00:12:37,820
Poor boy.

175
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:41,250
He won't die a decent death
at Linie's hands.

176
00:12:43,270 --> 00:12:44,720
One more question.

177
00:12:45,450 --> 00:12:47,230
Where is Frieren?

178
00:12:50,110 --> 00:12:52,010
She fled the town

179
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:56,310
because you killed the dungeon guard.

180
00:12:56,770 --> 00:12:59,570
Graf Granat said something similar.

181
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:02,280
Killing a guard is a serious crime, it seems.

182
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,240
The punishment is execution.

183
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:05,570
Execution?

184
00:13:06,230 --> 00:13:09,660
That wouldn't be enough
to make that woman flee.

185
00:13:10,210 --> 00:13:13,550
She holds a powerful grudge against demons,

186
00:13:14,070 --> 00:13:18,600
enough to teach her own student
a spell purely for demon-killing.

187
00:13:20,190 --> 00:13:22,670
Someone like that wouldn't run.

188
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:25,470
She must be after something.

189
00:13:28,310 --> 00:13:29,590
It must be Lady Aura.

190
00:13:33,670 --> 00:13:35,480
Don't move.

191
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:40,300
You know where Ms. Frieren
is headed, don't you?

192
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:42,700
You're wasting your time.

193
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:46,900
You lied about failing to kill me.

194
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:51,990
You wanted revenge for my surprising you.

195
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,390
You're proud and arrogant.

196
00:13:55,850 --> 00:14:01,080
You still don't see us—see anyone
besides Ms. Frieren as a threat.

197
00:14:02,110 --> 00:14:05,180
That's why you granted me an opportunity.

198
00:14:07,530 --> 00:14:11,170
From this distance, I can blast
a hole clean through your heart.

199
00:14:12,690 --> 00:14:13,920
Try it.

200
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:16,850
Your head will fly before
you get the chance.

201
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:29,770
Ms. Frieren, am I useful?

202
00:14:29,770 --> 00:14:31,880
Why would you ask that?

203
00:14:33,470 --> 00:14:37,550
I'm not as good at magic as you are.

204
00:14:38,630 --> 00:14:41,840
I've lived for much longer than you.

205
00:14:42,190 --> 00:14:44,710
In that regard, you'll never catch up to me.

206
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:48,090
I see.

207
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:52,860
But that only applies to mana and technique.

208
00:14:53,670 --> 00:14:57,510
I often let you handle
battles against monsters.

209
00:14:57,510 --> 00:15:00,370
Yes, you've forced those on me many times.

210
00:15:00,370 --> 00:15:01,430
I'm sorry, okay?

211
00:15:02,590 --> 00:15:05,720
But battles end quicker when you fight

212
00:15:06,180 --> 00:15:09,220
because you fire off spells
faster than I do.

213
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:17,000
Girl, I have dedicated the majority
of my life to the pursuit of magic.

214
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:19,310
So have I.

215
00:15:33,850 --> 00:15:36,470
<i>How is she responding so quickly?</i>

216
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:41,690
<i>If I hadn't reflexively defended myself,
that would've pierced my heart.</i>

217
00:15:42,090 --> 00:15:43,920
You blocked it.

218
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:46,220
So your heart is your weak point.

219
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:48,730
<i>This girl...</i>

220
00:15:49,980 --> 00:15:51,230
I see.

221
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:55,480
You weren't lying about
dedicating your life to magic.

222
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:59,550
Then I shall crush you with all my might.

223
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:01,250
Balterie.

224
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:06,820
Sounds like they've begun as well.

225
00:16:08,330 --> 00:16:10,250
It's a shame, though.

226
00:16:10,710 --> 00:16:12,750
We're nearly finished here.

227
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:16,040
Perhaps I'll observe their battle.

228
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:20,090
Lord Lügner gets cross when I interfere.

229
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:26,520
Oh?

230
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:30,530
We're not finished yet.

231
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:34,280
You're tough. Perhaps I'll be
able to enjoy this a little.

232
00:16:38,010 --> 00:16:42,780
<i>My mana, technique, and control
are all far greater than hers.</i>

233
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:08,540
<i>This girl cannot compare to me.</i>

234
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:11,530
<i>However, she's fast.</i>

235
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:16,110
<i>I'm being overwhelmed by the sheer
number of attacks, pure and simple.</i>

236
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:27,310
<i>Damn you, Frieren.
How did you train this girl?</i>

237
00:17:31,430 --> 00:17:34,630
<i>I'll engage her in a battle of attrition
and wait for her to exhaust her mana.</i>

238
00:17:48,050 --> 00:17:49,150
<i>No, I can't.</i>

239
00:17:50,210 --> 00:17:52,600
<i>The battle will be over before then.</i>

240
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:56,210
<i>If I could just create an opening...</i>

241
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:59,430
Linie, what are you doing?

242
00:17:59,430 --> 00:18:01,170
Hurry up and defeat him!

243
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:10,330
Honestly, how selfish.

244
00:18:10,330 --> 00:18:13,090
He's refusing to do anything
but fight defensively.

245
00:18:31,810 --> 00:18:35,230
How are you wielding your axe like that?

246
00:18:35,230 --> 00:18:37,260
Those are my master's techniques.

247
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:40,900
I'm skilled at reading mana.

248
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:46,380
I memorize the flow of mana
inside a person when they move

249
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:48,470
and imitate their movements.

250
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:50,160
Just like this.

251
00:19:13,930 --> 00:19:17,740
I knew it from the first time I saw
your movements at the mansion.

252
00:19:18,370 --> 00:19:23,110
They're the same as those of the
powerful warrior I once memorized.

253
00:19:26,910 --> 00:19:29,060
Coincidences really do happen.

254
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:30,570
Fate is an interesting thing.

255
00:19:34,940 --> 00:19:36,330
You don't mean...

256
00:19:36,710 --> 00:19:40,090
I am imitating the movements
of Eisen the Warrior.

257
00:19:41,410 --> 00:19:44,070
<i>Seriously? This is crazy.</i>

258
00:19:47,170 --> 00:19:49,380
<i>I can't win this fight.</i>

259
00:19:58,160 --> 00:20:00,340
He finally fell.

260
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:02,050
I must hurry.

261
00:20:02,050 --> 00:20:04,250
Lord Lügner will be upset with me again.

262
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:11,930
<i>"Fell"? Have I fallen?</i>

263
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,580
Stand up, Stark.

264
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:22,560
No matter how battered you get,
you cannot fall.

265
00:20:23,370 --> 00:20:29,910
Yeah, but there's no way I can beat you.

266
00:20:30,380 --> 00:20:31,830
Of course you can't.

267
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:34,600
I'm stronger than you.

268
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:36,650
Then...

269
00:20:36,650 --> 00:20:40,290
But you got back up.

270
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:43,370
That means you haven't lost yet.

271
00:20:43,370 --> 00:20:44,980
What kind of logic is that?

272
00:20:45,820 --> 00:20:50,790
Stark, I'll teach you the secret
to defeating powerful opponents.

273
00:20:51,540 --> 00:20:53,100
It's simple.

274
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:56,910
Keep getting back up and hitting them.

275
00:20:56,910 --> 00:21:01,760
For warriors, whoever's still standing
at the end is the winner.

276
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:08,580
Damn it, Master.

277
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:11,710
You and your weird logic.

278
00:21:12,130 --> 00:21:14,690
I guess your brain's made of muscles,
like the rest of you.

279
00:21:16,770 --> 00:21:19,700
You should've just stayed down.

280
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:21,430
You already lost.

281
00:21:22,290 --> 00:21:24,070
I'm still standing.

282
00:21:26,210 --> 00:21:28,420
Besides, I remember now.

283
00:21:28,420 --> 00:21:30,990
My master's blows were heavier.

284
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:35,290
Yours are just imitations after all.

285
00:21:40,370 --> 00:21:44,460
Then I will use those imitations
to send you to your end.

286
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:46,670
Erfassen.

287
00:21:47,190 --> 00:21:48,580
Balterie!

288
00:22:00,770 --> 00:22:03,380
<i>A wide swing, with no regard for defense.</i>

289
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:04,790
<i>He's lost his mind.</i>

290
00:22:12,630 --> 00:22:16,390
I was prepared for us to kill each other,
but I shouldn't have been so scared.

291
00:22:16,390 --> 00:22:19,100
Your attacks don't have any
weight behind them at all.

292
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:22,830
Lightning Strike!

293
00:22:34,980 --> 00:22:35,970
Linie!

294
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:37,180
Shi—

295
00:22:37,180 --> 00:22:38,630
Zoltraak.

296
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:46,520
<i>Demon-killing magic...</i>

297
00:22:50,030 --> 00:22:52,570
<i>And you alright</i>

298
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:55,080
<i>Can you hear me</i>

299
00:22:55,870 --> 00:23:01,960
<i>Trailing along deserted train tracks</i>

300
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:04,290
<i>Crying excessively</i>

301
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:07,460
<i>Wanting you to smile</i>

302
00:23:07,460 --> 00:23:13,510
<i>I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh</i>

303
00:23:13,510 --> 00:23:17,220
<i>There's something I'd like to tell you</i>

304
00:23:17,220 --> 00:23:19,980
<i>With words more precious than a goodbye</i>

305
00:23:19,980 --> 00:23:25,650
<i>Unremarkable yet special</i>

306
00:23:25,650 --> 00:23:29,190
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

307
00:23:29,190 --> 00:23:32,240
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

308
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:36,990
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

309
00:23:36,990 --> 00:23:43,080
<i>So, if I were to be born again</i>

310
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:48,920
<i>I would surely choose this place once more</i>

311
00:23:48,920 --> 00:23:54,930
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

312
00:23:54,930 --> 00:24:00,680
<i>I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present</i>

313
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:03,650
<i>Even if no promises were made</i>

314
00:24:03,650 --> 00:24:06,570
<i>Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness</i>

315
00:24:06,570 --> 00:24:12,740
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

316
00:24:12,740 --> 00:24:15,410
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby</i>

317
00:24:15,410 --> 00:24:19,330
<i>for you to come back home</i>

318
00:24:20,150 --> 00:24:21,750
She has roughly one-fifth of my mana.

319
00:24:20,260 --> 00:24:23,150
I've heard there's a long-lived
mage in these woods.

320
00:24:21,770 --> 00:24:23,720
If she engages her directly,
Frieren will lose.

321
00:24:23,610 --> 00:24:25,780
You are no match for me.

322
00:24:23,610 --> 00:24:26,250
What do you think, Heiter?

323
00:24:24,460 --> 00:24:25,660
It's an elf village.

324
00:24:25,660 --> 00:24:27,700
Kill all the elves.

325
00:24:25,780 --> 00:24:30,010
Because you're a far more powerful mage.
